From 6a00516b70e8a72c4386d8b2f27b1a471bf12c67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James <spadent@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:21:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Faster soft stretch: column table, each source row built
 once

The per-pixel 64-bit division was a __divdi3 call on 32-bit x86. Columns
now come from a cached table, and each distinct source row is scaled once
into a RAM row and copied to every screen row that shows it, so the
framebuffer is only written. Output is pixel-identical (new test).
